01:04:20.498 --> 01:04:23.324
grounds could not be RAP tax is my guess. That's it. Right.

01:04:23.774 --> 01:04:27.035
That could still be RAP tax. You can use it to fund operations.

01:04:27.341 --> 01:04:30.682
Oh, okay, there you go. Yeah, you actually could. My question

01:04:31.182 --> 01:04:34.860
with that would be we're currently developing a process by which people apply for RAP

01:04:35.360 --> 01:04:39.182
tax funding. Is this something that would need to go through that process for things

01:04:39.682 --> 01:04:43.102
like this? I don't think that it should. I've seen that other cities,

01:04:43.600 --> 01:04:47.438
Lehi specifically, There's a chunk of that money that

01:04:47.534 --> 01:04:50.986
the city designates to go toward projects that they've

01:04:51.066 --> 01:04:54.758
heard from the community broadly need

01:04:55.258 --> 01:04:57.744
to be done and taken care of in their parks. And then there's a chunk

01:04:58.244 --> 01:05:02.287
of their rat tax that the community service or rat board goes

01:05:02.319 --> 01:05:05.658
through and makes determinations and awards grants and different things

01:05:05.674 --> 01:05:08.948
like that. I think that there will be certain things

01:05:09.446 --> 01:05:12.979
that we as a body who has that responsibility over

01:05:13.140 --> 01:05:16.742
all budget and all funds to say, yep, this chunk is

01:05:16.774 --> 01:05:20.280
gonna go to take care of some of those needs that have been

01:05:21.266 --> 01:05:25.472
identified by the Community Services Board and identified by

01:05:25.972 --> 01:05:29.355
listening to residents and still meet

01:05:29.855 --> 01:05:33.728
that objective of letting the people on the Community Services Board be able

01:05:34.228 --> 01:05:36.309
to weigh in on how those funds are used.

01:05:37.800 --> 01:05:40.398
I think that's kind of, that's one of the things that I've said for a

01:05:40.898 --> 01:05:44.400
long time is, I like that they've come with the initiative of these are some

01:05:44.675 --> 01:05:48.341
kind of low-hanging fruit, as I would call it, that we can do. Like the

01:05:48.841 --> 01:05:52.755
Smith Ranch benches can be funded with sponsorship

01:05:52.771 --> 01:05:55.993
money, but that it's— we can do

01:05:56.493 --> 01:06:00.337
this with all kinds of different funds, and that's up to us to

01:06:00.837 --> 01:06:02.879
