01:07:30.020 --> 01:07:33.473
our— that's already budgeted for. And so I, I don't

01:07:33.973 --> 01:07:36.637
think we have to go to the level that like we want benches there and

01:07:37.137 --> 01:07:40.219
we have to go to a memorial program. I'm not saying that you, you can't.

01:07:40.717 --> 01:07:43.929
You guys could develop a memorial program and that's something that we could implement.

01:07:44.475 --> 01:07:48.234
But I think we could get some benches in sooner with some of those

01:07:48.266 --> 01:07:51.543
funds. The other thought that I have is I think it's going to be good

01:07:52.043 --> 01:07:55.701
to go out and obviously assess the parks and whatnot. We do have

01:07:55.798 --> 01:07:58.945
our asset management program that we've been trying to get

01:07:59.009 --> 01:08:02.605
all of our data into, and that's playgrounds, benches, everything.

01:08:03.344 --> 01:08:06.892
And one thing that we gotta be aware of is sometimes, you know, we're gonna

01:08:07.392 --> 01:08:10.810
make large purchase scale items like playgrounds and whatnot,

01:08:11.468 --> 01:08:14.567
but we have to be protective that we wanna try to use those out for

01:08:14.583 --> 01:08:19.078
their useful life. And that's part of what this asset management program's And

01:08:19.578 --> 01:08:22.948
so as we see things in disrepair or whatnot, we definitely want to know about

01:08:23.448 --> 01:08:27.171
those things. But then we have to weigh it against the overall condition of it

01:08:27.283 --> 01:08:31.137
and a replacement schedule of it as well. And so there will be some balance

01:08:31.637 --> 01:08:35.392
as we work through that. We're willing and we're trying to develop

01:08:35.892 --> 01:08:39.743
that, and it's getting a little bit better each day. Obviously, our playgrounds,

01:08:39.791 --> 01:08:42.890
our benches, our trash cans, our pavilions, and all those things—the high,

01:08:43.276 --> 01:08:46.229
the most visual things are the first things that we put in there and we're

01:08:46.729 --> 01:08:50.241
trying to manage that. But what that's gonna do is that's gonna kick out a

01:08:50.741 --> 01:08:53.371
maintenance or a replacement schedule long-term too.

01:08:54.173 --> 01:08:56.709
And we have to be careful. And the other thing I wanna bring up is

01:08:57.608 --> 01:09:00.721
after these amenities are installed,

01:09:01.556 --> 01:09:05.087
