01:42:43.490 --> 01:42:47.102
We know e-bikes and scooters are becoming more and more popular in our communities,

01:42:47.215 --> 01:42:50.988
especially with our kids. Unfortunately, we're seeing a significant

01:42:51.488 --> 01:42:54.665
increase in the number of injuries with riding e-bikes

01:42:54.681 --> 01:42:57.138
and scooters. We want to get your attention.

01:42:57.635 --> 01:43:01.232
E-bikes and e-scooters are not toys. They are vehicles.

01:43:02.549 --> 01:43:06.129
Here at Unified Fire Authority, we want to make sure that everybody understands

01:43:06.145 --> 01:43:09.854
the risks of riding, knows how to ride safely, and has the proper

01:43:10.354 --> 01:43:12.536
safety equipment and wears it every time they ride.

01:43:13.949 --> 01:43:17.128
Riding a traditional bike requires physical effort to build speed.

01:43:17.626 --> 01:43:21.223
E-bikes and e-scooters are different. They provide a lot more power

01:43:21.560 --> 01:43:25.060
with little to no effort, making it easier to reach higher

01:43:25.108 --> 01:43:29.460
speeds. That combination of speed and minimal effort

01:43:29.508 --> 01:43:32.623
can make it harder to recognize how much risk you're taking

01:43:32.880 --> 01:43:36.558
and how quickly things can change. More speed means

01:43:36.654 --> 01:43:40.125
less time to react, which can lead to very serious

01:43:40.205 --> 01:43:44.784
injuries, especially when not wearing a helmet. In 2025

01:43:45.284 --> 01:43:50.087
alone, Intermountain Healthcare emergency rooms across Utah treated 536

01:43:50.587 --> 01:43:54.762
people for e-bike and e-scooter injuries. Furthermore, only about 40%

01:43:54.987 --> 01:43:58.345
of bike trauma patients were wearing a helmet at the time of their crash.

01:43:59.165 --> 01:44:03.148
A new state law is now in effect requiring e-bike and e-scooter riders

01:44:03.260 --> 01:44:06.648
under 21 to wear an approved helmet when riding on public

01:44:06.713 --> 01:44:09.860
roads. Ideally, a full-face helmet, which offers the

01:44:10.360 --> 01:44:13.183
most protection. These statistics are concerning,

01:44:13.456 --> 01:44:17.278
but there are steps we can take to avoid many of these accidents and injuries.

01:44:17.888 --> 01:44:21.164
So, what can we do about it?

01:44:21.469 --> 01:44:25.210
Parents, pay close attention to the e-bikes and scooters your child

01:44:25.258 --> 01:44:27.876
is riding. Make sure it's appropriate for their age.

01:44:28.712 --> 01:44:31.154
Helmet on every ride, every time,

01:44:31.765 --> 01:44:35.380
no exception. Teach your kids to follow traffic laws and

01:44:35.880 --> 01:44:39.607
signs, ride at a safe speed, and always stay alert to what's happening

01:44:39.719 --> 01:44:43.383
around them. At intersections and crosswalks, teach them

01:44:43.495 --> 01:44:47.159
to yield to drivers and pedestrians, never blow through an intersection,

01:44:47.416 --> 01:44:50.823
and make sure both parties can see each other before proceeding.

01:44:51.980 --> 01:44:56.186
Make sure they're wearing visible clothing and have proper lights, especially in low-light

01:44:56.686 --> 01:45:00.682
conditions. These simple steps can help keep our kids safe

01:45:00.827 --> 01:45:04.889
every time they ride. Remember, e-bikes and scooters are

01:45:04.937 --> 01:45:08.277
not toys. They are vehicles. So let's all work together

01:45:08.694 --> 01:45:11.858
to make sure that our kids make it home safely every time.

