volunteer opportunities in their local communities, helping people find ways to serve.

01:50:02.098 --> 01:50:05.255
According to their interests, abilities, and availability, and whereas

01:50:05.431 --> 01:50:09.677
Eagle Mountain City desires to encourage and strengthen volunteerism

01:50:09.693 --> 01:50:13.187
throughout the community and to help residents discover opportunities

01:50:13.283 --> 01:50:16.456
to serve their neighbors and improve the quality of life in Eagle Mountain,

01:50:17.369 --> 01:50:20.894
and whereas the city recognizes that service is most

01:50:21.394 --> 01:50:25.445
powerful when residents, organizations, businesses, and community partners

01:50:25.878 --> 01:50:28.169
work together toward the common good,

01:50:29.165 --> 01:50:33.066
And whereas designating Eagle Mountain City as a JustServe City

01:50:33.820 --> 01:50:38.075
demonstrates the city's commitment to promoting volunteerism,

01:50:38.556 --> 01:50:42.618
connecting residents with opportunities to serve, and supporting organizations

01:50:42.730 --> 01:50:45.829
that seek to make a positive difference in our community.

01:50:46.647 --> 01:50:50.725
Now therefore, be it proclaimed that Mayor Jared

01:50:50.757 --> 01:50:54.241
Gray and the Eagle Mountain City Council do hereby

01:50:54.369 --> 01:50:57.891
designate Eagle Mountain City as a JustServe

01:50:57.923 --> 01:51:01.013
city and encourage residents, organizations,

01:51:01.078 --> 01:51:04.377
businesses, and community partners to participate

01:51:04.877 --> 01:51:07.515
in meaningful service opportunities throughout our community.

01:51:08.194 --> 01:51:10.327
Dated this 15th day of September,

01:51:10.456 --> 01:51:11.599
2026.

01:51:14.014 --> 01:51:17.813
OK, thank you, Craig. Marcus, just as a reminder,

01:51:18.103 --> 01:51:20.361
proclamation executive, or do we need to accept that by motion?

01:51:24.244 --> 01:51:27.664
I think historically we have just done it as

01:51:27.761 --> 01:51:30.828
an executive proclamation. Okay.

01:51:31.390 --> 01:51:35.259
Well, it's included in the consent agenda, isn't it? Or no? No.

01:51:35.468 --> 01:51:37.732
Okay. That's why I was wondering if it needed to be.

01:51:38.454 --> 01:51:42.372
Just executive? I think that's what we've done historically. I think we should continue

01:51:42.872 --> 01:51:45.327
with what we've always done. Okay, be it done.

01:51:47.029 --> 01:51:51.059
Um, next item is, uh, public comment.

01:51:51.300 --> 01:51:54.495
Time has been set aside for the public to express their ideas, concerns,

01:51:54.511 --> 01:51:57.738
and comments. As a reminder, public comment is an opportunity for the

01:51:58.238 --> 01:52:01.640
community members to address the city council, and each speaker is allowed up

01:52:02.140 --> 01:52:04.916
to 3 minutes. If you wish to speak during the public comment portion,

01:52:05.590 --> 01:52:09.155
please complete the comment form located in the back of the room and return

01:52:09.187 --> 01:52:11.017
it to our city recorder, Lacey, on this side.

01:52:14.623 --> 01:52:17.808
Council members will listen but not engage in discussion during public comment.

01:52:17.905 --> 01:52:19.707
We ask that everyone remain respectful.

01:52:21.299 --> 01:52:25.749
Disruptive behavior, including cheering, booing, clapping, or comments directed

01:52:26.249 --> 01:52:30.033
at individual city employees, is prohibited. If you have an issue or question regarding

01:52:30.533 --> 01:52:34.274
staff or personnel, administrative staff will meet you in the foyer for further discussion.

01:52:35.103 --> 01:52:38.274
Lastly, public comment period is for items not associated with

01:52:38.774 --> 01:52:42.007
the scheduled public hearing. If your comment relates to a public hearing item,

01:52:42.071 --> 01:52:45.221
please wait until that item is called. And tonight's public

01:52:45.721 --> 01:52:49.623
hearing items are 16A, resolution and public hearing of Eagle

01:52:50.123 --> 01:52:54.749
Mountain City approving the first amendment to the fiscal year 2026-2027

01:52:54.845 --> 01:52:58.637
annual budget. So that one we will call in just a few minutes.

01:52:59.361 --> 01:53:03.667
Right now I will open the public comment period at 7:16 and

01:53:04.020 --> 01:53:08.011
ask if if there's anyone here. I do have Brianne Salazar.

01:53:08.706 --> 01:53:12.166
She noted 16A but also wanted to comment on 17A.

01:53:12.602 --> 01:53:13.912
16A is a public hearing.

01:53:17.172 --> 01:53:21.515
OK, 16A we can wait, but 17A is fine.

01:53:22.136 --> 01:53:27.022
Brianne Salazar.

01:53:29.109 --> 01:53:31.902
We will allow you to come back again on 17, just so you know.

01:53:31.967 --> 01:53:34.641
You get 3 minutes, but in the public hearing you'll you'll get a chance again.

01:53:34.755 --> 01:53:37.344
So you will get a chance to speak again in '16.

01:53:40.312 --> 01:53:42.836
Make sure the mic is on. There you go.

01:53:43.225 --> 01:53:46.219
Okay, so I am Brianne Salazar.

01:53:47.336 --> 01:53:49.665
So I just have a couple of questions,

01:53:50.490 --> 01:53:53.384
and I know you can't answer my questions,

01:53:54.387 --> 01:53:57.656
but the one question that I have is, one,

01:53:57.990 --> 01:54:00.344
why do you think Do we pray?

01:54:01.810 --> 01:54:05.299
Why do we not have a clear designation of church and state?

01:54:07.615 --> 01:54:13.784
That is concerning to me as a non-prayerful

01:54:14.284 --> 01:54:18.125
person. That is troubling. Second,

01:54:18.690 --> 01:54:22.098
I just want to state that I hope or

01:54:22.550 --> 01:54:25.836
would ask that we do not. approve the

01:54:26.046 --> 01:54:29.333
property tax. And then I also

01:54:29.430 --> 01:54:33.229
ask that we stop having data

01:54:33.729 --> 01:54:37.459
centers come into Eagle Mountain. So as a resident

01:54:37.572 --> 01:54:40.865
that's just further up towards city center,

01:54:40.962 --> 01:54:44.838
I just ask that we stop having data centers come

01:54:44.903 --> 01:54:48.555
in. So that's all that I have.

01:54:48.635 --> 01:54:49.928
So thank you. Thank you.

01:55:00.251 --> 01:55:03.912
So Joy Rasmussen as well, general comments, and then the public hearing comment

01:55:04.008 --> 01:55:07.008
for 16A. Hello,

01:55:07.798 --> 01:55:11.419
I'm here once again to ask, I heard the news that Meta is

01:55:11.532 --> 01:55:15.010
building a bunch more data centers, and I'm not sure if those had been approved,

01:55:15.803 --> 01:55:19.007
like, a long time ago, or that was just like a recent thing.

01:55:20.146 --> 01:55:24.028
But the sentiment I'm hearing from everybody I know, most everybody, not everybody,

01:55:24.076 --> 01:55:27.557
but most everybody, is they're very concerned about building more and more data

01:55:28.057 --> 01:55:31.005
centers, that it's taking up so much land, and that's what we're going to be

01:55:31.505 --> 01:55:34.919
known for. That's going to affect our property values. There's lots of— it's very unpopular

01:55:35.419 --> 01:55:38.897
right now, data centers. And they're getting these deals

01:55:39.314 --> 01:55:42.474
to not pay very much property tax, which doesn't feel fair

01:55:42.538 --> 01:55:46.002
when you're raising it for us. And so I'm asking you again to

01:55:46.502 --> 01:55:49.801
please issue like a resolution that you

01:55:49.833 --> 01:55:53.136
will stop approving data centers until like

01:55:53.636 --> 01:55:56.294
safety measures have been taken to protect us. Like there's a lot of talk about

01:55:56.791 --> 01:56:00.558
AI being dangerous, and that's what these data centers are for. They're not for

01:56:01.058 --> 01:56:04.871
like just going on Facebook. They're all doing AI. And there's a

01:56:04.887 --> 01:56:08.462
lot of concerns about like the infrasound. So there's sound that you can't actually hear,

01:56:08.590 --> 01:56:12.233
but your body feels. And it damages your heart, people living near them are

01:56:12.282 --> 01:56:14.979
gonna be damaged by these data centers. It takes a bunch of energy,

01:56:15.718 --> 01:56:19.523
and it just feels kind

01:56:20.023 --> 01:56:22.606
of backwards to be raising our property taxes and giving these data centers the deals.

01:56:22.959 --> 01:56:26.636
So maybe if you were like publicly disclosed all the deals and showed the citizens

01:56:27.136 --> 01:56:30.458
like, hey, here's why they're benefiting us, like we've mentioned before, that might

01:56:30.506 --> 01:56:32.465
be a better way to do it before you announce a bunch of new data

01:56:32.497 --> 01:56:36.171
centers. Like, take citizens' input. And the second thing is

01:56:36.267 --> 01:56:39.777
I'm going to ask that you repeal the property tax increase because,

01:56:40.434 --> 01:56:44.905
um, we haven't been given the line-by-line budget numbers

01:56:45.081 --> 01:56:48.494
properly. Um, the pamphlet is inaccurate that we were given by

01:56:48.767 --> 01:56:52.500
the city. Um, the pamphlet says it would be on the ballot August 27— August

01:56:52.532 --> 01:56:56.330
of 2027, but the code says it should be on this coming November election if

01:56:56.378 --> 01:56:59.663
it gets enough signatures. So that's inaccurate. We've emailed the, the recorder

01:57:00.163 --> 01:57:02.240
to ask you to correct the pamphlet. I'm asking you guys to respond to that

01:57:02.740 --> 01:57:05.404
email and correct the— there's a lot of things that are inadequate or inaccurate according

01:57:05.421 --> 01:57:08.650
to law. So that's all I have to say. Thank you.

01:57:15.610 --> 01:57:16.013
Missy Perry.

01:57:19.520 --> 01:57:22.735
Just kind of piggybacking off of Joy Rasmussen,

01:57:22.752 --> 01:57:26.461
my name is Missy Perry. This is the first meeting

01:57:26.494 --> 01:57:30.286
I've come to. I've I've lived here for about 6 years,

01:57:30.462 --> 01:57:34.154
and I feel like you need to represent

01:57:34.654 --> 01:57:38.472
the citizens and also listen to the concerns

01:57:38.520 --> 01:57:42.003
that we have. And I find it incredibly concerning what has

01:57:42.035 --> 01:57:44.009
been happening recently in our city.

01:57:45.069 --> 01:57:48.247
I would like there to be a clear,

01:57:48.616 --> 01:57:51.248
concise outline of the budget,

01:57:52.292 --> 01:57:55.919
of the allocations of funds regarding our budget, and why the

01:57:56.419 --> 01:58:00.317
property tax increase has occurred. I want that to be put

01:58:00.478 --> 01:58:03.592
on the ballot to be voted on or either repealed

01:58:03.624 --> 01:58:07.075
because citizens have a right to choose. This is affecting

01:58:07.139 --> 01:58:10.767
my family. This is going to affect my future children. And I

01:58:11.267 --> 01:58:14.283
just want to see on the budget, I want to see the proof of your

01:58:14.783 --> 01:58:17.943
work. Where did you come up with this? What did you— did you look into

01:58:18.232 --> 01:58:21.811
other budgets to cut things, to kind of cut

01:58:21.859 --> 01:58:25.625
the fat to put money into other things to allocate

01:58:26.125 --> 01:58:30.285
that to help with what we need for public safety.

01:58:30.949 --> 01:58:35.835
Because I'm not against public safety or anything, even though that's been purported

01:58:36.108 --> 01:58:40.014
like throughout the media. Like, that's— I want to support

01:58:40.223 --> 01:58:43.367
the fact that we have an increased need for public,

01:58:44.726 --> 01:58:48.611
um, like police or a couple more deputies and whatnot.

01:58:48.692 --> 01:58:52.367
However, I want to see the proof of your work. I want to see

01:58:52.656 --> 01:58:55.225
where on the budgets we couldn't cut things. So,

01:58:56.189 --> 01:58:59.899
um, I want a line-by-line thing. I would like to see something similar

01:59:00.399 --> 01:59:03.657
to what, um, Saratoga Springs has and what

01:59:04.157 --> 01:59:07.560
they have shown their citizens. And I find it very concerning that every time

01:59:07.608 --> 01:59:11.511
it's brought up, it's deleted from the city citizens page. It's deleted,

01:59:12.089 --> 01:59:15.285
um, on all these different forums where usually

01:59:15.317 --> 01:59:18.883
we all come together and It's just very concerning to me that this is

01:59:18.931 --> 01:59:22.796
happening here in our town, and I'm

01:59:22.844 --> 01:59:26.078
having to come here in person

01:59:26.578 --> 01:59:30.060
and say, please just show me your work, show me the physical proof,

01:59:30.174 --> 01:59:33.152
because the links that are provided are not adequate at all.

01:59:33.832 --> 01:59:34.367
Thank you for your time.

01:59:38.595 --> 01:59:41.975
I do want to clarify that she did also request 16A, so we'll come

01:59:42.475 --> 01:59:43.206
back And that's all I have right now.

01:59:45.845 --> 01:59:49.219
Okay, is there anyone else that is here that came to speak in

01:59:49.719 --> 01:59:53.012
our public comment period that did not get

01:59:53.512 --> 01:59:57.997
an opportunity? Seeing no one, we will close our public comment period at 7:23,

01:59:59.127 --> 02:00:02.542
and we'll bring it back to the council. But I can answer a couple

02:00:03.042 --> 02:00:05.828
of quick questions. Marcus can help me on some of this.

02:00:06.022 --> 02:00:10.046
The question about the ballot. The county

02:00:10.062 --> 02:00:13.368
required— they're already printing ballots. They get mailed out in a couple

02:00:13.868 --> 02:00:16.980
of weeks. For us to say whether or not the referendum would be—

02:00:17.124 --> 02:00:19.660
would have the signatures on the ballot, we don't know that answer yet.

02:00:20.206 --> 02:00:23.432
So what the law actually says is that we can

02:00:23.544 --> 02:00:26.994
hold a special election. Yeah, it says that it'll be held the next

02:00:27.494 --> 02:00:30.991
regular municipal election, whichever is earlier, unless a special election is called.

02:00:31.761 --> 02:00:35.084
So the intent would be to call a special election In the event it qualifies

02:00:35.100 --> 02:00:38.697
for a ballot, right? There's no way to get it on the ballot because

02:00:38.713 --> 02:00:42.117
we don't have the signatures yet, and it's already required to be into

02:00:42.617 --> 02:00:45.938
the county right now. So given the signatures, it will be an item that

02:00:46.438 --> 02:00:49.423
will be voted on. It'll just be voted on at the appropriate time with the

02:00:49.923 --> 02:00:54.641
next election. I think that's

02:00:55.364 --> 02:00:57.660
most of what I'm going to address right now. I'm happy to address any of

02:00:58.160 --> 02:01:01.579
the other concerns or questions. After the meeting, so with that,

02:01:01.627 --> 02:01:06.452
we'll bring it back to the council and Melissa Councilman

02:01:06.952 --> 02:01:10.253
Clark. Thanks, Mayor. Thank you for being here tonight. It's fun to

02:01:10.269 --> 02:01:13.922
see first responders and some of our residents coming and sharing their

02:01:14.035 --> 02:01:17.753
thoughts about what's going on with the city and the questions that they have.

02:01:20.134 --> 02:01:23.542
If I could, I would sit down with you each on your front porch and

02:01:23.558 --> 02:01:27.220
talk to you about some of the decisions. decisions that we've made and help

02:01:27.720 --> 02:01:31.115
you see just some of our reasons behind them.

02:01:32.400 --> 02:01:37.053
So if you have questions, please reach out. It's very difficult to conduct

02:01:37.553 --> 02:01:40.672
a conversation on Facebook with people. So,

02:01:42.282 --> 02:01:45.792
um, that— I also want to thank our tiny,

02:01:45.824 --> 02:01:49.849
tiny army of staff that has done so

02:01:50.349 --> 02:01:54.350
many great things this summer with us. Between water

02:01:54.850 --> 02:01:59.002
pipes busting and wells going down and having

02:01:59.034 --> 02:02:02.960
to write and do huge packets and

02:02:05.256 --> 02:02:09.346
to do the publicity and information

02:02:09.443 --> 02:02:12.850
about different events and answer questions. And I

02:02:13.350 --> 02:02:17.012
really wanted to acknowledge Evan Barrett. 10 years

02:02:17.060 --> 02:02:20.445
ago, our city had an intern that thought

02:02:20.945 --> 02:02:24.363
it would be a really cool idea to have a street fair so

02:02:24.863 --> 02:02:27.735
that there would be a place for our small businesses to be able to go

02:02:28.361 --> 02:02:30.834
and sell what they make to our neighbors.

02:02:31.653 --> 02:02:35.105
And that street fair grew to the point where it didn't fit on the street

02:02:35.121 --> 02:02:38.766
anymore. And it was really, really cool. We liked

02:02:38.878 --> 02:02:41.415
that street because it was shaded and there were lots of trees there.

02:02:42.507 --> 02:02:46.505
But this weekend That street fair celebrated

02:02:47.005 --> 02:02:50.937
its 10th anniversary, and, um, none of that would have happened

02:02:51.437 --> 02:02:55.561
without Evan Barrett's dedication and foresight and

02:02:55.674 --> 02:02:59.013
drive to help support our small businesses in our community.

02:02:59.607 --> 02:03:03.076
And Evan, I just want to thank you for all that you've done to help

02:03:03.204 --> 02:03:06.576
economic development and our small businesses. So thank you.

02:03:09.804 --> 02:03:13.242
Thanks, Mayor. Welcome. It's good to see so many who've come

02:03:13.742 --> 02:03:17.484
out tonight. Just want to express my gratitude to each of you for taking

02:03:17.500 --> 02:03:20.007
the time to come and to share your thoughts. Even if we have a difference

02:03:20.507 --> 02:03:23.316
of opinion or we understand things perhaps from a little different perspective,

02:03:23.959 --> 02:03:27.687
I'm always grateful to, to have those who see things

02:03:27.719 --> 02:03:30.177
differently to help me see things from a different perspective.

02:03:31.173 --> 02:03:34.387
I want to, uh, I, I want to, I want to highlight Mayor Gray.

02:03:34.692 --> 02:03:37.400
He's not expecting this, He doesn't know this. I'm probably going to embarrass him,

02:03:38.562 --> 02:03:40.677
and I'm going to do it on purpose, okay?

02:03:43.476 --> 02:03:46.908
I just want to express my gratitude for the work that he has been doing.

02:03:47.650 --> 02:03:50.728
He has been running around Utah.

02:03:51.800 --> 02:03:55.341
He's been running around the nation and meeting with anybody

02:03:55.373 --> 02:03:58.931
and everybody whose ear he can get to try and help

02:03:58.979 --> 02:04:02.201
us advance those things that matter to Eagle Mountain. Citizens.

02:04:02.314 --> 02:04:05.814
He spent some time— and look,

02:04:05.830 --> 02:04:09.555
I know there are some who will say, well, gosh, why are you doing

02:04:09.604 --> 02:04:13.313
that? We're doing it because we're trying to improve our situation. I know

02:04:13.813 --> 02:04:16.974
he's met with Senator Curtis, with Congressman Kennedy.

02:04:18.226 --> 02:04:21.887
Certainly he met with the Speaker of the House today, Mike Schultz, and he's talked

02:04:22.387 --> 02:04:27.009
with Stuart Adams, our Senate President, worked with our local

02:04:27.586 --> 02:04:31.001
representatives, both House and Senate. And I just,

02:04:32.091 --> 02:04:35.746
I don't think the citizens really see the work that goes

02:04:35.778 --> 02:04:39.177
into what our mayor does. He's a cowboy at

02:04:39.225 --> 02:04:43.297
heart. He's used to getting up at 4:00 AM and taking clients

02:04:43.797 --> 02:04:46.471
on a hunt. And he works hard all day.

02:04:46.760 --> 02:04:50.142
He rides his horse, which anybody that's ridden a horse knows how

02:04:50.206 --> 02:04:53.975
much fun that is or isn't. I don't

02:04:54.475 --> 02:04:57.489
do it, can't do it. Some of you here do and enjoy that.

02:04:58.067 --> 02:05:02.111
But I just, I wish that each of you could spend 24

02:05:02.223 --> 02:05:05.529
hours with him and just see the effort that he's putting forth on your

02:05:06.029 --> 02:05:10.359
behalf. I think that the way you feel about him and perhaps this council would

02:05:10.859 --> 02:05:14.002
start to change and modify a little bit if you really understood the

02:05:14.179 --> 02:05:17.404
work that we are about. So thank you, Mayor Gray, for your

02:05:17.904 --> 02:05:21.993
leadership, your example, and for your advocacy. advocacy, and in

02:05:22.026 --> 02:05:25.184
spite of your many imperfections, which are

02:05:25.281 --> 02:05:28.826
smaller than mine, I just am grateful for you and

02:05:29.326 --> 02:05:30.205
for the efforts you've been putting forward.

02:05:34.420 --> 02:05:38.666
Thank you for those who made public comment. One invitation

02:05:39.166 --> 02:05:42.249
I'll extend is I'm very happy to meet with any of you who have concerns

02:05:42.749 --> 02:05:46.560
or questions that were brought up. It would be a lot easier to to

02:05:46.576 --> 02:05:49.592
go through and answer the questions in person,

02:05:50.667 --> 02:05:54.341
on Zoom, whatever, live. It'd be a lot easier than

02:05:55.336 --> 02:05:59.186
in an email or text messaging or definitely, or like

02:05:59.686 --> 02:06:03.085
instant messaging, whatever it may be. And I've extended that invitation to any who's had

02:06:03.117 --> 02:06:06.422
questions. Some residents have taken the opportunity to meet with me.

02:06:06.952 --> 02:06:09.567
And those of you who presented today, I'm happy to meet with you as well

02:06:10.096 --> 02:06:13.981
to ensure that your questions are all answered. and that

02:06:14.109 --> 02:06:17.433
understanding could be provided back and forth.

02:06:17.545 --> 02:06:21.238
So I'm very happy to listen and to share

02:06:21.738 --> 02:06:24.080
what I can. So just reach out to me individually. I'm happy to set up

02:06:24.580 --> 02:06:27.564
a private, or you can make it public if you want to bring people as

02:06:27.597 --> 02:06:30.342
well, that's fine. I'm happy to meet with whoever you wanna meet with, so,

02:06:31.193 --> 02:06:33.987
or have come and join on that. Grateful to be part of this great city.

02:06:34.405 --> 02:06:36.524
And, you know, we,

02:06:39.060 --> 02:06:42.441
This city has significant opportunity,

02:06:42.861 --> 02:06:45.951
and in many ways there's a

02:06:46.451 --> 02:06:49.660
blank canvas before us more than any other kind of city that's here in Utah.

02:06:50.447 --> 02:06:53.566
