03:43:40.370 --> 03:43:43.660
one got, that one got moved? Yeah, it got shifted around. That's the chili cook-off?

03:43:43.949 --> 03:43:47.080
Yeah, they, they moved it to the end of October. I need to verify the

03:43:47.580 --> 03:43:50.355
date. Okay, I see October— sorry, October 26th is what I see on that.

03:43:50.644 --> 03:43:53.839
The September 28th I can remove off my calendar? Yep, take it off.

03:43:54.321 --> 03:43:57.147
They changed it. Okay, they switched it on us. Got it.

03:43:57.969 --> 03:44:01.765
And then just DRC. I hope each of you get

03:44:02.265 --> 03:44:06.271
a chance to sit on the DRC for a year. It will really increase

03:44:06.771 --> 03:44:10.054
your appreciation for what our staff does preliminarily before we

03:44:10.554 --> 03:44:14.222
ever see anything. Mayor kind of

03:44:14.254 --> 03:44:17.824
gave me an assignment since I'm an evangelist

03:44:17.856 --> 03:44:21.378
for UTA to meet with

03:44:21.540 --> 03:44:25.362
Chandler, who's their government and community outreach person.

03:44:25.475 --> 03:44:28.682
One of the issues that we found with UTA, the new on-demand system,

03:44:28.779 --> 03:44:32.469
is that the system won't take

03:44:32.969 --> 03:44:36.518
you more than 6 miles unless you're going to a transit station. Well,

03:44:36.534 --> 03:44:39.651
for anybody who lives in City Center and needs to get

03:44:40.151 --> 03:44:43.720
to a job at Ridley's or Walmart, you can't get there.

03:44:45.075 --> 03:44:49.351
And that's a problem for a city that spans from Cedar

03:44:49.851 --> 03:44:53.005
Hills to Provo. Thank you. So we are

03:44:53.119 --> 03:44:57.942
working with them to create some special

03:44:57.974 --> 03:45:01.333
points that could get them up to

03:45:01.349 --> 03:45:03.853
Walmart, and maybe Walmart's one of them, City Hall.

03:45:05.145 --> 03:45:07.986
That is something that we're working on. I had the opportunity to go to the

03:45:08.551 --> 03:45:12.714
kind of grand opening of On Demand, and that was really good because

03:45:13.391 --> 03:45:17.009
I made sure everyone who had anything to do with planning at UTA

03:45:17.256 --> 03:45:19.488
heard about the 6-mile limitation,

03:45:20.404 --> 03:45:23.952
and it was good. I got to be there to represent our city while mayor

03:45:24.080 --> 03:45:27.693
was in New York. I think it was when you

03:45:28.193 --> 03:45:31.627
were busy with that. No, I think you were gone because I

03:45:32.127 --> 03:45:35.930
remember telling the other mayors. Yeah, that one, that one I met with Chandler

03:45:36.139 --> 03:45:39.109
and he— and by the way, he gave me like 4 on-demand passes that I

03:45:39.609 --> 03:45:42.240
would offer to anybody that would try and use it or any of the council.

03:45:43.204 --> 03:45:47.057
One of the— so 9 miles to Saratoga, we've talked about, to the kind of

03:45:47.557 --> 03:45:50.750
employment center where Costco is. And I was asking that we bump

03:45:51.250 --> 03:45:54.460
that up to get a little further distance. And as long as they're not busy,

03:45:54.524 --> 03:45:57.446
they've kind of been pretty lenient on that 6 miles, but that's the rule.

03:45:57.992 --> 03:46:01.910
So we've gone to Skyler Beltran and asked him to expand that. And that's

03:46:02.410 --> 03:46:05.812
where I passed the baton. I didn't have the bandwidth for that one. Well,

03:46:06.630 --> 03:46:10.651
I also think that Part of the issue is that they have a limited number

03:46:11.151 --> 03:46:14.285
of vehicles that are in the system, and we are out here on the

03:46:14.301 --> 03:46:17.829
outskirts of it. If we can—

03:46:18.216 --> 03:46:20.944
16 vehicles, and I think they had 1,000 rides the first day.

03:46:21.348 --> 03:46:25.060
1,000 rides the first 9 days, but that's still a lot. Okay,

03:46:25.222 --> 03:46:28.379
yeah, they gave me some stats. I was like, yeah, it was good. 'Cause at

03:46:28.879 --> 03:46:31.508
the grand opening, they announced that it was 1,003 rides.

03:46:34.344 --> 03:46:38.890
I think one thing that we as a city may need to consider is

03:46:39.549 --> 03:46:43.436
finding funding or getting support from some

03:46:43.936 --> 03:46:48.415
of the corporate partners within our boundaries to help fund additional

03:46:48.479 --> 03:46:51.756
vehicles that are— will help staff

03:46:51.916 --> 03:46:55.514
up more of the Eagle Mountain side of things

03:46:56.028 --> 03:46:59.257
so that they can't say we don't have enough vehicles to

03:46:59.757 --> 03:47:02.624
do that. This. So we'll go through the hoops of trying to get them to

03:47:03.233 --> 03:47:06.728
add miles for us and add additional locations that

03:47:06.840 --> 03:47:10.351
we can go to. But if that fails, which I'm

03:47:10.383 --> 03:47:13.701
not completely convinced that it will

03:47:13.749 --> 03:47:17.613
pass, like UTA has kind of let us down in the past,

03:47:17.998 --> 03:47:20.563
if that's the case, then I think we as a council and a city need

03:47:21.063 --> 03:47:24.458
to look at whether or not we seek funds from someone

03:47:24.506 --> 03:47:28.566
or some entity to help pay for that because it's a huge benefit

03:47:29.224 --> 03:47:33.044
to our residents. Council Member Wright just talked about our seniors,

03:47:34.280 --> 03:47:38.116
Council Member Whiting talked about our youth. Everyone is

03:47:38.616 --> 03:47:42.369
using this on demand and it's had a huge turnout. So I think it's something

03:47:42.869 --> 03:47:45.595
for us just to think about. They said a lot of the kids, like kids

03:47:45.611 --> 03:47:48.516
getting off of football practice because the buses have already left, have been using it.

03:47:49.303 --> 03:47:51.678
So one of the other things that I think we could advocate, and we could

03:47:52.178 --> 03:47:55.609
use the public to help us with this, is it's kind of meant

03:47:56.109 --> 03:47:58.978
for those first and last miles to get you home from a bus stop or

03:47:59.478 --> 03:48:02.925
something. But what would help is they will only do 6

03:48:03.425 --> 03:48:07.000
miles in those cases, like, you know, to your home. But if

03:48:07.016 --> 03:48:10.433
we identify Costco and Walmart and the high school,

03:48:11.011 --> 03:48:15.006
they'll do 10 miles if it's one of, you know, a specific location.

03:48:15.102 --> 03:48:18.728
Right. So we're trying to identify and employment areas. Exactly. I think

03:48:18.792 --> 03:48:22.562
the inherent problem with their 6-mile limitation, Mayor, is that the

03:48:23.062 --> 03:48:26.845
whole thing— the reason why they justified doing on-demand instead of

03:48:26.925 --> 03:48:30.502
the bus route that they came and announced to us and said that they were

03:48:31.002 --> 03:48:35.074
bringing and then pulled back— is that they want to find ridership

03:48:35.574 --> 03:48:39.405
numbers. Well, if there's a third of our population is

03:48:39.905 --> 03:48:43.674
outside of that 6-mile limit to get to Walmart or any other employment employment

03:48:44.174 --> 03:48:47.861
centers, that means 1/3 automatically isn't going

03:48:48.361 --> 03:48:51.822
to be factored into ridership numbers because it's not useful to them. And I think

03:48:52.322 --> 03:48:55.724
that we have to be a squeaky wheel with this. And you

03:48:55.740 --> 03:48:59.568
picked the right person to send. I was just going

03:49:00.068 --> 03:49:03.655
to note that I got a call from Bob Allen with MAG letting

03:49:03.687 --> 03:49:07.613
me know that Saratoga Springs and UTA are applying

03:49:07.726 --> 03:49:11.897
for UDOT innovation grant money in order to expand and extend that

03:49:12.315 --> 03:49:15.703
6-mile limit, and, and they wanted to know if Eagle Mountain

03:49:16.203 --> 03:49:19.556
wanted to join in on that same application. I thought so. I know

03:49:20.056 --> 03:49:23.506
that I sent something in to Mayor and Ben, and I think

03:49:23.635 --> 03:49:27.681
that you guys had talked about Kimberly was going to have our grant writer

03:49:28.181 --> 03:49:31.663
start looking at that. That deadline's coming up, and I don't want us to miss

03:49:32.163 --> 03:49:36.014
out on it. When they had told me about it, there was only one other

03:49:36.514 --> 03:49:40.173
city that had even submitted anything, and I know that Saratoga is doing it

03:49:40.189 --> 03:49:43.561
too. We have a stronger case if we do something with them, I think.

03:49:44.187 --> 03:49:47.655
Um, I, I had a meeting with Mark Christensen as well, and, um,

03:49:48.137 --> 03:49:51.493
he, he encouraged us to put in an application. He thought that it

03:49:51.993 --> 03:49:55.250
would be more beneficial. You can go up to $3 million per application,

03:49:55.668 --> 03:49:58.702
and if we join in, then of course we're limited,

03:49:58.799 --> 03:50:01.976
but there's an opportunity for both cities to put put in and potentially get $6

03:50:02.008 --> 03:50:05.247
million for our region. So he encouraged us actually to do it

03:50:05.747 --> 03:50:08.999
separately and try to meet that timeline. I think we could have a whole other

03:50:09.499 --> 03:50:12.751
fleet with that amount of money. Does it say— is it $6

03:50:13.251 --> 03:50:16.455
million in a year or $3 million in a year? I don't know

03:50:16.955 --> 03:50:20.432
the specifics. Those are just numbers he provided. The grant's a 3-year funding,

03:50:21.169 --> 03:50:25.081
so that number is probably a 3-year number total. But then,

03:50:25.434 --> 03:50:28.128
then we would have to decide at that point whether we want— whether we have

03:50:28.144 --> 03:50:34.022
some other funding Or we ask a corporation

03:50:34.055 --> 03:50:37.835
to do a match. Or we petition

03:50:37.932 --> 03:50:41.391
UTA to bring our own tax dollars back because we are already paying for those

03:50:41.891 --> 03:50:45.675
dollars. That too. Of course,

03:50:45.691 --> 03:50:49.709
you know, you've heard a lot of my reports with UFA and at the Capitol,

03:50:49.823 --> 03:50:53.376
just different things I've got going. So unless you have specific questions,

03:50:53.473 --> 03:50:56.767
I won't bore you with my 40 hours by Monday.

03:50:57.461 --> 03:51:00.123
Mayor, can you, and maybe you talked about it and I just missed it,

03:51:00.155 --> 03:51:04.108
did you talk at all about where we're at with UTA and the process

03:51:04.156 --> 03:51:07.546
that we're trying to get figured out with UTA, not UTA,

03:51:08.012 --> 03:51:11.869
UFA and UFSA and where we're

03:51:11.885 --> 03:51:16.189
at with that? I met with them this morning and that we're

03:51:16.689 --> 03:51:18.608
90% on the contract. She said she'll have it this week.

03:51:20.022 --> 03:51:23.999
Yeah, that's what she indicated to me was that she's 90% finished with the draft

03:51:24.512 --> 03:51:28.200
for me to review. Yep, that's what she said. And then we're working through

03:51:28.700 --> 03:51:31.825
the tax code to try to figure out how to make sure that

03:51:32.129 --> 03:51:35.561
we don't overtax in the transition or

03:51:36.061 --> 03:51:39.586
undertax in the transition. And I think we got it figured out today, some solutions,

03:51:39.650 --> 03:51:42.922
but it's more about also working with the state on

03:51:43.018 --> 03:51:46.129
how to pull those funds in and to do it properly.

03:51:46.964 --> 03:51:50.994
We've seen where mistakes have been made in other counties. So that's

03:51:51.042 --> 03:51:54.735
really what the holdup. But right now, the answer to your question is December 31st,

03:51:54.751 --> 03:51:57.192
2027. Right.

03:51:58.203 --> 03:52:01.350
And we're also working with the league. We met with the league this week as

03:52:01.415 --> 03:52:04.915
well to— because while it would

03:52:04.947 --> 03:52:08.560
be an increase to our taxes, it would be a decrease to UFA

03:52:09.060 --> 03:52:13.056
taxes. And the net effect is zero to our residents. And so Ultimately, it should

03:52:13.556 --> 03:52:18.215
not trigger truth in taxation. It should be a net zero

03:52:18.263 --> 03:52:21.541
to the residents. And is there a possibility for

03:52:21.637 --> 03:52:25.333
legislative changes that would allow for that? Logan ran into a very similar

03:52:25.349 --> 03:52:28.531
issue this year between the county that was providing a service and a city,

03:52:29.029 --> 03:52:32.114
and they ran into that issue and it became— it got onto

03:52:32.614 --> 03:52:36.099
the state's radar. We believe that that

03:52:36.599 --> 03:52:39.857
would be very important for ARC. Thank you. because truth in taxation

03:52:39.890 --> 03:52:43.133
should just be that, truth. And the truth is your

03:52:43.165 --> 03:52:46.794
taxes wouldn't go up, it would just be transferring from one to another.

03:52:46.938 --> 03:52:51.097
And the interesting thing is that the House rep, the rep that runs

03:52:51.370 --> 03:52:55.272
a lot of the tax bills is in Logan. So it's

03:52:55.930 --> 03:52:59.976
hopefully that it's on his radar. Well, I think it's

03:53:00.025 --> 03:53:03.091
just like with the school districts. We have Alpine School District,

03:53:03.477 --> 03:53:06.838
as a taxing entity right now. The Lake Mountain School District doesn't have

03:53:06.870 --> 03:53:10.262
to do a truth in taxation to switch and bring that over. So I think

03:53:10.762 --> 03:53:14.318
I'm glad you guys are pursuing that. That's what we're working

03:53:14.334 --> 03:53:17.698
on. So yeah, lots of meetings. We've met with the league,

03:53:17.714 --> 03:53:21.482
we've met with the state, we met with all those people this week. It's been

03:53:21.514 --> 03:53:23.550
busy. It's Tuesday. Yes.

03:53:23.696 --> 03:53:26.055
Anything else?

03:53:27.655 --> 03:53:31.519
Yep. Go ahead. Mayor, I move that,

03:53:31.583 --> 03:53:37.362
uh, we adjourn to a closed session for the purpose of discussing,

03:53:38.360 --> 03:53:42.160
uh, discussion of pending or reasonable imminent litigation, the character,

03:53:42.403 --> 03:53:45.702
professional competence, or physical or mental health of an individual,

03:53:45.718 --> 03:53:49.611
the purchase, lease, sell, or exchange of real property, a proposed

03:53:49.659 --> 03:53:54.029
development agreement, project proposal, or financing proposal related

03:53:54.529 --> 03:53:57.867
to the development of land owned by the estate or political subdivision

03:53:58.365 --> 03:54:01.801
and/or the deployment of security personnel, devices, or systems pursuant

03:54:01.833 --> 03:54:05.173
to Section 52-4-205,

03:54:05.269 --> 03:54:08.336
Subsat 1 of the Utah Code Annotated. Second.

03:54:09.299 --> 03:54:12.591
All right, we do have a motion by Councilmember Wright and a second by Councilmember

03:54:13.091 --> 03:54:16.429
Whiting, and we will return to this meeting afterwards to adjourn, just so you're

03:54:16.445 --> 03:54:19.511
aware. We'll start the vote with Councilmember Clark. Yes.

03:54:19.736 --> 03:54:22.454
Councilmember Wright. Yes. Councilmember Whiting? Yes.

03:54:22.793 --> 03:54:26.484
Okay, at 9:17 we'll go to closed session. Sometimes I think

03:54:26.984 --> 03:54:30.239
it's good to read those so that the public understands the things that we can

03:54:30.288 --> 03:54:31.728
address. It's what we just learned.

